course: dictionary
lesson: 8246
title: Rhino: a big animal, or old money?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rhino is a very large, heavy animal with thick skin and one or two horns on its nose. When a word has more than one meaning, read the sentence to find the right one. «Werribee near Melbourne and Monarto in South Australia are huge open-range zoos where herds of giraffes, rhinos and zebras roam large areas» tells you rhinos are animals, because they are listed with giraffes and zebras and they roam.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If "animal" still makes sense where the word is, you have found the right meaning. «Rhino» can also mean money in old UK slang, but you will rarely hear that now, so in most texts it is the animal.
explain: Look for clues about size and behaviour. «The Parsee takes his revenge» is a story about a rhino, and it is strong and heavy, so the clues help you picture it. Even when a text is funny or made up, the clues can still tell you what a rhino is.
fact: Rhino is short for rhinoceros.
fact: A rhino is a large, heavy, thick-skinned animal with one or two horns on its nose.
fact: Rhinos live in Africa and southern Asia, and they eat plants such as grass, leaves and shoots.
fact: Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same stuff as your hair and nails.
fact: Rhinos are endangered because poachers kill them for their horns, which have no real medical power.
exercise: «Rhinos eat only plants: grass, leaves, shoots.» What do rhinos eat? | Cake | *Plants such as grass and leaves | Fish | Meat from other animals
exercise: Which of these describes a rhino? | *A large, heavy animal with thick skin and a horn on its nose | A small, quick bird with bright feathers | A tall tree with thin branches | A soft toy with a long tail
exercise: «Herds of giraffes, rhinos and zebras roam large areas.» What does roam mean? | Sit still and quiet | *Wander freely over a wide area | Fly high in the sky | Sleep all day in a small box
test: Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same stuff as hair and nails. What is keratin made of? | Glass | Metal | *It is the same stuff as our hair and nails | Sugar and water
test: Nadia reads «rhino» in an old book and it means money. Which is true? | It means a type of tree | *It is an old UK slang meaning for money, now rarely heard | It means a kind of cake | It means a small fish
exam: Why are rhinos in danger? | Because people keep them as pets in their homes | Because they cannot swim | *Because poachers kill them for their horns | Because they are too small to find food
